  "foaf:name": "Silent Depth under the Arctic Ocean",
  "sdo:name": "Silent Depth under the Arctic Ocean",
  "sdo:description": "&quot;Silent Depth under the Arctic Ocean&quot; is a science-sailing initiative by PVO Expeditions in collaboration with Tarevoktere to address Arctic kelp forest decline. Through bi-annual expeditions in northern Norway, we will map kelp density, test urchin-removal techniques, and document restoration efforts. The project blends research, exploration, and media to generate open-access data, visual content, and policy advocacy. The aim is to raise awareness of the hidden crisis facing Arctic marine ecosystems, engage local and global communities, and contribute to long-term kelp forest regeneration and climate resilience.",
